From 4325b49035b613d5564f858f2a15217bd0b52fdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marius Gehrmann <marius@gehrmann.solutions>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:40:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] drm: apple: Let the J613 internal pipe drive a Type-C
 display, lid closed

With the lid closed and two external displays, macOS drives the second
one with the internal DCP's pipe (IOMFBIntDcpUsedForExtWhenLidClose):
the panel is off, and the pipe's first DPTX core is free for the
left-front USB-C port. When the lid opens, the pipe goes back to the
panel. Do the same on J613, where the internal pipe has a Type-C route
to that port (dcp->clamshell).

Fabric. The internal pipe counts as busy unless the lid is closed and
the panel and its CRTC are off (dcp->clamshell_free). While it is free
it ranks as a plain pipeline, before dcpext: with the panel's connector
disconnected, aquamarine (Hyprland) gives a display coming up on the
left-front port the lowest free CRTC it can use, the internal pipe's,
and the route follows that pairing (routed to dcpext instead, every mode
failed the atomic check, and the panel found its only CRTC taken on lid
open). When the pipe becomes free it takes a display left waiting, as
any pipeline that is let go of (dcp_typec_pipeline_changed()). When the
lid opens, that display lets go of the pipe first (powered off, HPD
dropped, route taken down), then IOMFB is told; the display goes to
dcpext if dcpext is free, or waits again with the usual log line.

Lid open, order. The panel's connector comes back once the compositor
switched the pipe's CRTC off, or two seconds later, and at once if the
CRTC was off already. A left-front display that leaves the pipe for a
free dcpext reads disconnected until then (at most 3 s) and is reported
200 ms after the panel, so that the compositor gives the panel its CRTC
back and the display dcpext's.

Session. Once the panel has started, the DPTX endpoint is started for
the route, and the DPAV controller endpoint with it, as for the T6030
external processors. The DPTX RemotePort unit 0 (core 0, crossbar
dispext0,0) is DPTX port 0; the panel's own DPTX port is never bound.
The link is connected as on the T8122 dcpext (dcp_ext_dptx_607()), the
same firmware image. Call 25, which the firmware sends to each
RemotePort when the lid state changes, is acknowledged quietly. While
the route is active (v14->typec) the session handles the display
description as on an external processor; the mode is set with A472(1)
before A411 (A411 first leaves "Modeset done, but pipe not enabled"),
its CRTC off powers it off (A472(0)), swaps are sized to its mode
without notch rows or the panel's colour matrix, and a refused swap does
not end the session. When the route is taken down, the panel's one mode
is the pipe's catalog again.

Other machines are unchanged, and so is J613 without the route.

